{:db/id 17592186096610 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186096410 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb40a0ff-c3b5-512d-a436-cc2fce456008" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Constant"}] :question/id #uuid "8e4367b2-f7bc-5588-b30b-d612915e3e68" :question/math-academy-id "e-3624" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=3e^x + \\ln 3$, find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $e^x$ is just $e^x$ itself. On the other hand, $\\ln 3$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nUsing the addition rule, then, we have \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nf'(x) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(3e^x + \\ln 3\\right)\\\n                                                  &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( 3e^x\\right) +  \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( \\ln 3 \\right)\\\n                                                  &= 3\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(e^x\\right) + 0\\\n                                                  &= 3 e^x.\n}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb40a0ff-c3b5-512d-a436-cc2fce456008" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048932}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186097160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb40a0ff-c3b5-512d-a436-cc2fce456008" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Constant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf8a11fa-1240-537a-95d9-4f13df04cb91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = \\ln 7 \\cdot e^{x}" :db/id 17592186094934} {:answer/id #uuid "dda24f68-a7ba-5bf1-96f0-617b7c17fe44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 7e^{x} + \\ln 7" :db/id 17592186094935} {:answer/id #uuid "1309387e-621f-5d0b-bfb6-5f115748360a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 0" :db/id